# Flutter Performance

Performance optimization must be evidence-driven.

Prefer const widgets, small widget trees, lazy lists, efficient keys, and avoiding unnecessary rebuilds.

For large collections use ListView.builder or equivalent lazy builders. Avoid expensive calculations inside build() and duplicate network requests caused by rebuilds.

Do not perform expensive synchronous work on the UI thread. Use appropriate async/isolate mechanisms when necessary.

When claiming a performance improvement, prefer evidence from Flutter DevTools, frame metrics, memory profiling, network measurements, startup time, or benchmarks.
